---
description: Help a new user create a Wireline account and build their first voice agent through the remote MCP server. Apply when the user mentions Wireline, voice agents, receptionists, or connecting Cursor to Wireline.
alwaysApply: false
---

Wireline MCP lives at `https://trywireline.com/mcp`. Authentication is OAuth against a real Wireline account. New users must create that account during Connect. Do not ask for API keys or paste secrets into config.

This is not a software development kit for embedding Wireline voice agents in another repository. The goal is a Wireline account plus a first voice-agent draft that lives in Wireline.

When the user wants a voice agent, use Wireline tools. If they have no agents, create the first draft after you summarize identity, goal, rules, and action boundaries and they explicitly confirm. To rehearse, run `run_private_agent_turn` or `start_private_voice_simulation`. Those are private rehearsals. Live calling, messaging, number attachment, billing, and launch stay in Wireline. Never claim those side effects completed here.

Training facts and rules land in Wireline only after the owner enables connected-app Training writes in Apps and confirms the write. If `train_wireline_agent` fails closed, send them to `/settings/apps#chatgpt-mcp`.

For status questions, prefer `get_wireline_agent_status` or `get_wireline_workspace_summary`. Do not request customer identities, transcripts, recordings, or phone numbers from MCP.
